A||N||3||WhiteFieroBlur||oil pressure gauge gone mad||||1||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||11-24-2001||04:26 AM||||Well when my car is nice and warmed up at idle my needle goes from 700 -1000 rpms back and forth also my oil pressure does the wiper thing going back and forth like crazy. When I step on the brake it seems to go crazy but when I let off it doesn't. It doesn't seem like its gonna die on me and the oil light doesn't go on, but my idle sure does go kinda low to scare me. is the idle suppose to be constant at like 1000rpm and not move? and what causes my oil pressure needle to go wacko on me? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-24-2001||06:08 AM||||Your idle will fluctuate 50-100rpms or so.  This seems to be normal.  The easy fix for the oil pressure gauges dance is to replace your sending unit.  Be smart and buy OEM.  I've had plenty of aftermarket sending units go out, but I've never had any trouble with my OEM one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||11-24-2001||10:07 AM||||Check your IAC valve and the MAP sensor. Either one of these will affect your idle speed. The oil pressure will vary widely when engine is searching for a correct idle speed.<BR>Hope this helps.<P>OOPS!<BR>Look for vacumn leaks also!<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 11-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-24-2001||01:07 PM||||Before replacing parts, any parts, check for vac leaks like Indy said. Also get the charging system checked. It's a free check at allot of places. call around.<P>next check battery and ground wires and all the other stuff in the wire service article in my cave. Multiple problems like that often mean one or more bad gound straps.<P>After all that is 100% checked out then, and only then, start looking at replacing parts.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
